## 8. Running the Project

### Backend
```bash
cd backend
# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
# Start server (port 5000)
python main.py
```

### Frontend
```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev   # Starts on http://localhost:5173
```

### Train Model (optional)
```bash
cd backend
python train_model.py
```

---

## 9. Known Limitations & Improvement Areas

| Area | Current State | Suggested Improvement |
|------|--------------|----------------------|
| Skin Classes | Only 3 (acne, normal, oily) | Expand to 10+ disease classes |
| Auth | Dual system (local + Supabase) can be fragmented | Unify to single Supabase auth |
| Model Accuracy | MobileNetV2 with small dataset | Fine-tune with larger dermatology dataset |
| OCR Accuracy | Tesseract performs poorly on curved/low-res labels | Add image super-resolution pre-processing |
| CORS | Hardcoded to `localhost:5173/5174` | Move to environment variables |
| JWT Secret | Hardcoded in source code | Move to [.env](file:///c:/Users/savan/Desktop/herbal/backend/.env) |
| Production Build | No deployment config present | Add Docker + CI/CD pipeline |

---

## 10. Summary

HerbHacks successfully demonstrates a working end-to-end AI-powered herbal skin care assistant with:
- ✅ Real-time skin type classification using transfer learning
- ✅ Herbal remedy recommendations
- ✅ OCR-based harmful ingredient detection
- ✅ Supabase-backed scan history and image storage
- ✅ Interactive nearby store map
- ✅ Secure JWT authentication
- ✅ Modern React SPA with glassmorphism UI

> Built for **CVMU Hackathon 4.0** — March 2026
